# Patch 0003: prompt routing — slash commands vs. path-leading messages.
#
# Applied last, on top of 0001 and 0002. Two independent defects:
#
#   1. extractSlashCommand treated any prompt whose trimmed text starts with
#      '/' as a slash command, so a Paseo message beginning with an absolute
#      path failed the whole prompt with -32602 and never reached the model.
#      Detection now mirrors the registry grammar and only routes names the
#      session actually exposes; everything else is an ordinary message.
#   2. runSlashCommand passed the abort signal as the registry's 'images'
#      argument (rc.8 order is agent, line, images, signal), leaving
#      invocation.signal undefined: every registered command died with
#      'Internal error: command failed: Cannot read properties of undefined
#      (reading aborted)'.

